 14. SPARSE LUCAS-KANADE -- binCV cuda::calcOpticalFlowPyrLKAsync
     vs cv::cuda::SparsePyrLKOpticalFlow (cudaoptflow)
=====================================================================
 ROLE: 'track a keypoint set from one frame to the next over a
 pyramid, on device'. BOTH SIDES' PYRAMIDS ARE RESIDENT AT ENTRY
 and neither arm builds one inside the bracket -- cv::cuda's
 calc() overload that takes std::vector<GpuMat> pyramids is used
 for exactly that reason, so the row is a like-for-like rather
 than a subtraction estimate.
 SAME WINDOW BOTH SIDES: 31x31, 4 levels, iteration cap 20,
 err off on both, both free-running (cv::cuda breaks on its own
 0.01-pixel convergence test; binCV on its own epsilon rule --
 forcing equal iteration counts would be forcing a DIFFERENT
 algorithm on one of them).
 keypoints: 204 at the reference minDistance of 33.33 px, 2048 at
 6 px, both from goodFeaturesToTrack on frame 0 of the REAL
 sequence.

