 sparse LK tracker resident state (both frames at every level + keypoint arrays)  [752x480]  -- METER 2 on BOTH sides (cudaMemGetInfo delta),
 each side over enough independent working sets that the meter's
 2.00 MB unit resolves, then divided by its own count.
   [meter 2] cv::cuda       44.00 MB over   32 sets =    1408.0 KB/frame  (22 units)
   [meter 2] binCV          42.00 MB over   96 sets =     448.0 KB/frame  (21 units)
   [meter 2] ROUNDING: one 2.00 MB unit is 21.3 KB/frame at 96 sets (4.76% of binCV's
             figure) and 64.0 KB/frame at 32 sets (4.55% of OpenCV's).
   ratio OpenCV/binCV = 3.143x  -- binCV is SMALLER by 3.143x.
   The OpenCV side is an UPPER BOUND: GpuMat pads its pitch, and any
   filter buffer or NPP scratch held past the call is inside this
   delta. binCV's side is cudaMalloc with nothing in between.
