             figure) and 64.0 KB/frame at 32 sets (4.55% of OpenCV's).
   ratio OpenCV/binCV = 3.143x  -- binCV is SMALLER by 3.143x.
   The OpenCV side is an UPPER BOUND: GpuMat pads its pitch, and any
   filter buffer or NPP scratch held past the call is inside this
   delta. binCV's side is cudaMalloc with nothing in between.
